{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-dee3c511d859d93bf9d9","statement":"Of course, one can define another sheaf theory $\\sshv$ and its constructible version $\\scshv$ for prestacks by right Kan extension of <<ref:eq-*-pullback-ind-constructible>> and <<ref:eq-six-operation-*-constructible>> along $(\\qcsp_k)^{\\op}\\subset (\\prestk_k)^{\\op}$.\nBy definition, is a canonical equivalence\n\n\\begin{equation}\n\\cshv(X)\\cong \\scshv(X)^{\\op},\n\\end{equation}\n\nbut $\\shv(X)$ and $\\sshv(X)$ are in general unrelated.\nThe theory $\\sshv$ has its own applications.\nBut <<ref:colimit.sheaves.pseudo-proper.stacks>> is the main reason we would like to work with the sheaf theory $\\shv$ in this work.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"96d1c4bb582d8969bbe910f890b0287a911f9711962299cf04c303c62af129ce","kind":"remark","label":"Remark 778","ref_key":"shv over sshv","name":"","order":1097,"deps":[{"ref":"colimit.sheaves.pseudo-proper.stacks","card_id":"ma-c-73b8d2f94c2184da7815","label":"Corollary 777","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"eq-*-pullback-ind-constructible","card_id":"ma-c-63852803896ffdddac18","label":"Equation eq-*-pullback-ind-constructible","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"eq-six-operation-*-constructible","card_id":"ma-c-a5c80dd70e209c209f35","label":"Equation eq-six-operation-*-constructible","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1b700e8c4a2fc6f0c0f522039f223820ba6737a9a0ac91aea37c58ba7a3389c2","line":20376,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-28T11:10:54+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":608,"math_hints":34}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","title":"Tame categorical local Langlands correspondence","abstract":"In one 